-- Design Warning Section

attribute DESIGN_WARNING of XCVN3408_VSVB2197 : entity is
 "The Versal ACAP device contains two JTAG TAPs in series: " &
        "1. the Arm DAP, and " &
        "2. the main device_package TAP. " &
        "See the JTAG and Boundary-Scan section in the Xilinx Versal ACAP " &
        "Technical Reference Manual (AM011) at https://www.xilinx.com " &
        "for details. " &
        "To correctly model the JTAG chain of devices in a JTAG boundary-scan test tool, " &
        "each physical Versal ACAP device instance in the JTAG schematic " &
        "must be replaced/represented by the following two virtual JTAG devices: " &
        "1. Arm DAP    versal_net_arm_dap.bsd for Versal Net (XCVN) devices " &
        "           or versal_arm_dap.bsd     for all other Versal devices; " &
        "2. Versal device_package.bsd file. " &
    "This BSDL file is a device model of a fully-powered and UNCONFIGURED device. " &
        "The functions described in this BSDL file are available when all of the " &
        "conditions listed in the BSDL file header comments are met, including: " &
        "device fully-powered; device is unconfigured; free-running clock to REF_CLK; " &
        "POR_B pin is High; and device JTAG interface is not secured/protected. " &
        "Otherwise, if the listed conditions are not met, then one or more functions " &
        "described in this BSDL file might not be available or the IDCODE " &
        "reported by the device might be invalid. " &
        "Recommended: Keep the device unconfigured during boundary-scan to " &
        "ensure device JTAG behavior matches this BSDL device model by setting " &
        "the inputs to the device MODE[3:0] pins to 0000 (the JTAG boot mode " &
        "setting) before power-on (or at least before and through the Low-to-High " &
        "transition of the input to the POR_B pin. " &
    "All IOBs prior to configuration, and unused and output-only IOBs following " &
        "configuration, will sense their pad values during boundary-scan with an " &
        "LVCMOS-type input buffer. An input voltage level that does not meet the " &
        "LVCMOS input-High or input-Low requirement might not be captured as " &
        "'1' or '0', respectively. For post-configuration boundary-scan only: " &
        "If an IOB is configured to use an input standard that uses VREF pins, " &
        "then the boundary-scan test vectors must keep the used VREF pins 3-stated.";

end XCVN3408_VSVB2197;

